# Design System

The app should feel friendly, modern, educational, and human.

It should NOT visually imitate a dating app.

## Visual hierarchy

Every screen should have:
1. clear page purpose
2. primary content
3. primary action
4. secondary actions

Avoid excessive cards, borders, shadows, and decorative gradients.

## Typography

Use the project's typography tokens.
Do not hardcode random font sizes across screens.

Prefer semantic names such as:
- display
- title
- heading
- body
- label
- caption

## Spacing

Use shared spacing tokens.
Do not invent one-off margins repeatedly.

## Colors

Use semantic tokens:

```text
background
surface
surfaceElevated
textPrimary
textSecondary
textMuted
border
primary
primaryForeground
success
warning
error
```

Do not hardcode colors in every component.

## Components

Buttons must communicate hierarchy:
- primary
- secondary
- tertiary/destructive

Inputs should clearly show:
- label
- value
- validation state
- disabled state
- focus state

## Accessibility

- Minimum comfortable touch target.
- Support dynamic font sizing where feasible.
- Provide accessible labels for icon-only buttons.
- Ensure contrast.
- Respect reduced-motion settings when practical.
- Do not communicate errors only through color.
